  "theory": {
"intro": "Two copies of a triangle can make a parallelogram: turn one copy around and join them. Each triangle has half the area of the parallelogram.

The shaded triangle is one of the two equal halves.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\normalsize}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (4.4,0);
\coordinate (C) at (5.8,2.6);
\coordinate (D) at (1.4,2.6);
\coordinate (H) at (1.4,0);
\fill[gray!20] (A) -- (B) -- (D) -- cycle;
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway,below] {$\text{base}$};
\draw (B) -- (C);
\draw (C) -- (D);
\draw (D) -- (A);
\draw (B) -- (D);
\draw[dashed] (D) -- (H) node[midway,right] {$\text{height}$};
\coordinate (ra) at ($(H)!0.3cm!(D)$);
\coordinate (rb) at ($(H)!0.3cm!(B)$);
\draw (ra) -- ($(ra)+(rb)-(H)$) -- (rb);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]",
"facts": [
"**Area $=$ base $\times$ perpendicular height $\div2$.**",
"Choose a side as the base. Its height is measured at a right angle from that base to the opposite corner.",
"The height may meet the base outside the triangle. Extend the base in a straight line to find it.",
"Use the height for the chosen base. A slanted side is not that height unless it meets the base at a right angle.",
"Area is measured in square units: cm$^{2}$, m$^{2}$.",
"For a cost, find the area, then multiply by the cost per square unit. Buy enough whole rolls or bags to cover all the area."
],
"steps": [
"Identify the base and its perpendicular height (at a right angle to the base or its extension).",
"Multiply base $\times$ height, then halve the result.",
"Write the answer with squared units."
],
"workedExamples": [
  {
    "question_text": "[tikz]
