Find the area of the triangle. The dashed line extends the base.",
    "solution_text": "Use the actual $9\text{ cm}$ base, not the base together with its extension. The perpendicular height is $6\text{ cm}$ even though it is outside the triangle. The slanted $10\text{ cm}$ side is not needed.
$\text{Area}=9\times6\div2$
$=54\div2$
$=27\text{ cm}^{2}$"
  },
  {
    "question_text": "[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\normalsize}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
