$=39\text{ cm}^{2}$
For any triangle, multiply its base by its perpendicular height, then halve the result."
  },
  {
    "question_text": "Triangle A has base $12\text{ cm}$ and perpendicular height $5\text{ cm}$. Triangle B has base $9\text{ cm}$ and perpendicular height $8\text{ cm}$. Which has the larger area, and by how many square centimetres?",
    "solution_text": "$\text{Area of A}=12\times5\div2$
$=30\text{ cm}^{2}$
$\text{Area of B}=9\times8\div2$
$=36\text{ cm}^{2}$
