  },
  {
    "question_text": "A triangular lawn has base $13\text{ m}$ and perpendicular height $6\text{ m}$. Each whole roll of turf covers $8\text{ m}^{2}$. How many rolls must be bought?",
    "solution_text": "$\text{Area}=13\times6\div2$
$=78\div2$
$=39\text{ m}^{2}$
$4\times8=32$
Four rolls leave $7\text{ m}^{2}$ uncovered.
$5\times8=40$
Buy $5$ rolls to cover all $39\text{ m}^{2}$."
  }
]
},
